'''Theophalus Curtis Ratliff'''<ref>{{Cite web|title=Theo Ratliff Stats|url=https://www.basketball-reference.com/players/r/ratlith01.html|access-date=2020-09-07|website=Basketball-Reference.com}}</ref> (born April 17, 1973) is an American former professional [[basketball]] player who played 16 seasons in the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA).

Born in [[Alabama]], Ratliff played for and graduated from the [[University of Wyoming]], before being selected by the [[Detroit Pistons]] in the [[1995 NBA draft]]. He also played for the [[Philadelphia 76ers]], the [[Atlanta Hawks]], the [[Portland Trail Blazers]], the [[Boston Celtics]], the [[Minnesota Timberwolves]], the Detroit Pistons, the [[San Antonio Spurs]], the [[Charlotte Bobcats]] and the [[Los Angeles Lakers]]. Primarily a [[Center (basketball)|center]], he was widely regarded as an excellent [[block (basketball)|shot-blocker]] and [[List of National Basketball Association annual blocks leaders|led the league three times in blocks per game]]. {{As of|2026}}, he was ranked [[List of NBA career blocks leaders|21st all-time in career blocks]].<ref>[https://www.espn.com/nba/history/leaders/_/stat/blocks ESPN.com - All-Time Leaders-Blocks<!-- Bot generated title -->]</ref>

