'''Timofey Pavlovich Mozgov''' ({{lang-rus|Тимофей Павлович Мозгов|p=tʲɪmɐˈfʲej mɐˈzɡof}}, born 16 July 1986) is a Russian former professional [[basketball]] player. He played eight seasons in the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA) between 2010 and 2018, playing for the [[New York Knicks]], [[Denver Nuggets]], [[Cleveland Cavaliers]], [[Los Angeles Lakers]] and [[Brooklyn Nets]]. In 2016, he won an [[NBA championship]] with the Cavaliers, becoming one of the first Russians to do so, alongside then-teammate [[Sasha Kaun]]. He returned to Russia in 2019 and retired from professional basketball in 2022.

As a member of the [[Russia national basketball team|Russian national team]], Mozgov won a bronze medal at both [[EuroBasket 2011]] and the [[Basketball at the 2012 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|2012 Summer Olympics]].
